====Adjective====
{{en-adj|farther,further|sup=+,farthermost,furthermost}}

# {{senseid|en|distant}} [[distant|Distant]]; remote in space.
#: {{ux|en|He went to a '''far''' land.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Joshua|9|6|passage=And they went to Ioshua vnto the campe at Gilgal, and said vnto him, and to the men of Israel, Wee be come from a '''farre''' countrey: Now therefore make ye a league with vs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009  |title=Racism Postcolonialism Europe |author=Graham Huggan; Ian Law |page=1 |ISBN=|passage=Tsiolkas's Europe, as voraciously predatory as his own undead protagonist, is a '''far''' cry from the fount of idealistic humanism dreamed up by generations of both pre- and post-Enlightenment politicians and philosophers, a Europe defined by its durable capacity for civility in an otherwise barbarous world.}}
# Remote in time.
#: ''the '''far far''' future''
# Long. {{rfex|en}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011| title=Ramblings from a Soul |author=Peggy Woods | page=42| passage=I have such a long way to go but yet I have come such a '''far''' piece already}}
# More remote of two.
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=19|passage=At the '''far''' end of the houses the head gardener stood waiting for his mistress, and he gave her strips of bass to tie up her nosegay. This she did slowly and laboriously, with knuckly old fingers that shook.}}
#: {{ux|en|See those two mountains? The ogre lives on the '''far''' one.}}
#: {{ux|en|He moved to the '''far''' end of the state. She remained at this end.}}
# Extreme, as measured from some central or neutral position.
#: {{ux|en|They are on the '''far''' right on this issue.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010| title=The City Is served Bartholomew! to the American Prison!|author=William Alexander Patterson, 4th | page=118| passage=He was withdrawn to such a '''far''' degree that it required of Piers and Jude a good deal of occasional conferencing between the two of them, in private. }}
# [[extreme|Extreme]], as a difference in nature or quality.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1657| title=The Art of Logick.|author=Henry Ainsworth; Zachary Coke| page=26| passage=As ''sensible'' maketh a man differ from a stone, in a '''far''' difference; for other Species, as Beasts, have the same difference, but reasonable is the nearest, whereby he differeth from a stone, beasts, and all other things.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1979| title=Military situation in the Far East - Volume 3 |author=United States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Armed Services, United States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Foreign Relations | page=1737| passage=Is there not a '''far''' difference between asking it up and urging it, Mr. Secretary?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010| title=Screen Adaptations: Jane Austen's Pride and Prejudice|author=Deborah Cartmell | page=78| passage=The pressbook identifies the film as a 'picturization of Jane Austen's widely read novel' and starring Greer Garson and Laurence Olivier (based on the theatrical adaptation by Helen Jerome), it is a '''far''' remove from adaptations that follow. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014| title=Playful Intelligence: Digitizing Tradition |author=Henry Sussman | page=124| passage=This may not be at such a '''far''' remove from the endlessly recursive textual inventions of Kafka, Beckett, and Bernhard as it may seem.}}
# {{lb|en|programming|not comparable}} Outside the currently selected [[segment]] in a segmented [[memory]] [[architecture]].
#: {{ux|en|'''far''' heap; '''far''' memory; '''far''' pointer}}

=====Usage notes=====
Comparable senses often repeat the adjective to intensify the meaning rather than using ''very'' as most other adjectives do. For example, one may speak of the {{good||'''far far future'''}} rather than the {{qmark||''very far future''}}.

