#* {{quote-text|en|year=1933|author=w:Dorothy L. Sayers|title=The Queen’s Square|passage=“I don’t like that young woman,” said Lady Hermione; she’s '''fast'''.” “Dear Lady!” “I’ve no doubt you think me old-fashioned. Well, I’m glad I am. I say she’s '''fast''', and what’s more, heartless. I was watching her before supper, and I’m sorry for Tony Lee. She’s been flirting as hard as she can go with Harry Vibart-not to give it a worse name-and she’s got Jim Playfair on a string too. She can’t even leave Frank Bellingham alone, though she’s staying in his house.”}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1979|author=w:Doug Fieger|title={{w|Good Girls Don't (song)|Good Girls Don't}}
