===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|fermen}}, from {{der|en|xno|fermer|t=to let out for a fixed payment, lease, rent}} ultimately from the same {{der|en|ang|-}} source as Etymology 1. Compare {{cog|ang|feormian|t=to feed, supply with food, sustain}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[work]] on a farm, especially in the growing and [[harvest]]ing of crops.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To devote (land) to farming.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To grow (a particular crop).
# To give up to another, as an estate, a business, the revenue, etc., on condition of receiving in return a percentage of what it yields; to [[farm out]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''farm''' the taxes}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=December 1, 1783|year_published=1855|speaker={{w|Edmund Burke}}|title=The Works of R.H. Edmund Burke|volume=2|chapter=Speech on Mr. Fox's East-India Bill|text=[The East-India Company] have contrived to '''farm''' their subjects, and their duties toward these subjects, to that very Nabob, whom they themselves constantly represent as an habitual oppressor and a relentless tyrant.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To [[lease]] or [[let]] for an [[equivalent]], e.g. land for a rent; to yield the use of to proceeds.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 2|I|iv|passage=We are enforced to '''farm''' our royal realm.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To take at a certain rent or rate.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1886|title=The Fortnightly|volume=46|page=530
|passage=In Paris it is stated that nearly half the birth-rate of the city finds its way to nurses who '''farm''' babies in the suburbs.}}
# {{senseid|en|gaming}}{{lb|en|internet slang|online gaming}} To engage in [[grinding]] (repetitive activity) in a particular area or against specific enemies for a particular [[drop]] or item.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|year=2004|author=Doug Freyburger|title=Pudding '''Farming''' Requires Care|newsgroup=rec.games.roguelike.nethack
|passage=When you hit a black pudding with an iron weapon that does at least one point of damage there is a good chance it will divide into two black puddings of the same size (but half the hit points IIRC). {{...}} When eaten black puddings confer several intrinsics so AC [armor class] is not the only potential benefit. {{...}} Since black puddings are formidible{{SIC}} monsters for an inexperienced character, '''farming''' is also a good way to die.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Robert Alan Brookey|title=Hollywood Gamers|page=130
|passage=The practice of gold '''farming''' is controversial within gaming communities and violates the end user licensing agreements{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|Internet}} To [[cultivate]] and/or [[disseminate]] through [[artificial]] [[algorithm]]-[[incentivize]]d means.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theverge.com/2023/1/19/23562966/cnet-ai-written-stories-red-ventures-seo-marketing|work={{w|The Verge}}|passage=This type of SEO '''farming''' can be massively lucrative. Digital marketers have built an entire industry on top of credit card affiliate links, from which they then earn a generous profit.|title=Inside CNET’s AI-powered SEO money machine|date=2023-01-19|author=Mia Sato; Vincent James|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261011052123/https://www.theverge.com/2023/1/19/23562966/cnet-ai-written-stories-red-ventures-seo-marketing|archivedate=11 October 2026}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.e-flux.com/architecture/intensification/6782975/eating-the-future-the-metabolic-logic-of-ai-slop|work={{w|e-flux}}|passage=Will AI slop '''farming''' ultimately exhaust the soil of online spaces? Will people flee the slop, tolerate it, or even welcome it? Will we ultimately come to love slop?|title=Eating the Future: The Metabolic Logic of AI Slop|date=2025-09|author=Kate Crawford|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260913210906/https://www.e-flux.com/architecture/intensification/6782975/eating-the-future-the-metabolic-logic-of-ai-slop|archivedate=13 September 2026}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/boazsobrado/2026/02/11/inside-the-clipping-farms-driving-fintechs-marketing-boom/|work={{w|Forbes}}|passage=X's suspension of the Stake-linked accounts and the UK Gambling Commission's enforcement action represent the first significant consequences for clip '''farming'''.|title=Inside The 'Clipping Farms' Driving Fintech's Marketing Boom|date=2026-02-11|author=Boaz Sobrado|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261002014227/https://www.forbes.com/sites/boazsobrado/2026/02/11/inside-the-clipping-farms-driving-fintechs-marketing-boom/|archivedate=2 October 2026}}
