===Etymology 1===
From {{der-lite|en|enm|fin}}, from {{der-lite|en|ang|finn}}, from {{der-lite|en|gem-pro|sc=Latn|*finnō}}, {{m-lite|gem-pro|sc=Latn|*finǭ||dorsal fin}} (compare {{cog-lite|nl|vin}}, {{cog-lite|de|Finne}}, {{cog-lite|sv|fena|finne, fena}}), from {{der-lite|en|ine-pro|sc=Latn|*(s)pīn-||backbone, dorsal fin}} (compare {{cog-lite|sga|ind||end, point}}, {{cog-lite|la|pinna||feather, wing, fin}}, {{cog-lite|xto|spin||hook}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q4162555}}{{lb|en|ichthyology|zootomy}} One of the [[appendage]]s of a [[fish]], used to [[propel]] itself and to [[manoeuvre]]/[[maneuver]].
#: {{ux|en|The fish's '''fins''' minimize water flow.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=4|passage=Then he commenced to talk, really talk. and inside of two flaps of a herring's '''fin''' he had me mesmerized, like Eben Holt's boy at the town hall show. He talked about the ills of humanity, and the glories of health and Nature and service and land knows what all.}}
# A similar appendage of a [[cetacean#Noun|cetacean]] or other [[marine]] animal.
#: {{ux|en|a dolphin's '''fin'''}}
# A thin, rigid component of an [[aircraft]], extending from the [[fuselage]] and used to [[stabilise]] and [[steer]] the aircraft.
#: {{ux|en|The '''fin''' stabilises the plane in flight.}}
# A similar structure [[protrude|protruding]] from a [[projectile]], used to help keep it on course.
# {{lb|en|surfing}} A similar structure on the bottom of a [[surfboard]], used to help steer it.
# A [[hairstyle]], resembling the fin of a fish, in which the hair is [[comb]]ed and set into a [[vertical]] [[ridge]] along the top of the head from about the [[crown]] to the [[forehead]].
# A device worn by [[diver]]s and [[swimmer]]s on their [[feet]].
#: {{ux|en|The divers wore '''fins''' to swim faster.}}
# An extending part on a [[surface]] of a [[radiator]], [[engine]], [[heatsink]], etc., used to [[facilitate]] cooling.
# A sharp [[raised]] [[edge]] (generally in [[concrete]]) capable of damaging a [[roof]] [[membrane]] or [[vapor retarder]].
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[conning tower]] of a [[submarine]].
# {{lb|en|UK|slang|obsolete}} A person's [[hand]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1839|title=Dearden's Miscellany|volume=1-2|page=661
|passage="Done say I to that, Reuben, tip me your '''fin''', my spark, and it shall be a bet."}}

