# [[especially|Especially]] or [[extraordinarily]] [[fine]] or [[pleasing]]; [[exceptional]].
#: {{ux|en|They sell good coffee and pastries, but their chocolate is '''exquisite'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Sourav Ganguly scored an '''exquisite''' century in his debut Test match.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1800|title=Reflections for Every Day in the Year on the Works of God, and of His Providence Throughout all Nature|author=Christoph Christian Sturm|publisher= D. Schaw and Company|isbn=|page=77|url=https://archive.org/details/reflectionsfore01sturgoog/page/n8/mode/2up?q=exquisite
|passage= For us the bee gathers, from the leaves of flowers, that '''exquisite''' honey destined for our use. For us the ox is put to the plough, and desires no other reward than a little food. It is also for us that the forests, the fields, and the gardens, abound in riches; the greatest part of which would be lost, if they were not of use to us. For us also are designed the treasures the mountains contain. It is true, that we have, beyond comparison, more wants than the brute creation ; but we have also, many more faculties, talents, and industry, to make every thing around us serve for our use and pleasure. Millions of creatures contribute towards our food, clothes, and habitations, and furnish us with innumerable conveniences and enjoyments.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|I|passage=Selwyn, sitting up rumpled and cross-legged on the floor, after having boloed Drina to everybody's '''exquisite''' satisfaction, looked around at the sudden rustle of skirts to catch a glimpse of a vanishing figure&mdash;a glimmer of ruddy hair and the white curve of a youthful face, half-buried in a muff.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=February 5, 1983|title=Yingko -- Taiwan's ceramics capital|journal=w:Arab News
|url=https://archive.org/details/ArabNews1983SaudiArabiaEnglish/Feb%2005%201983%2C%20Arab%20News%2C%20%2369%2C%20Saudi%20Arabia%20%28en%29/
